    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10328": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Immunology and Immunotherapy - 108289 - Grade 7",
      "description": "A post-doctoral research fellow position is available in the Fungal Immunology Group within the Institute of Immunology & Immunotherapy, College of Medical & Dental Sciences, University of Birmingham, led by Prof Rebecca Drummond. This role is to create and contribute to the creation of knowledge by undertaking a specified range of  activities within an established research programme and/or specific research project.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-22",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10327": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Immunology and Immunotherapy - 108301 - Grade 7",
      "description": "A post-doctoral research fellow position is available in the Fungal Immunology Group within the Institute of Immunology & Immunotherapy, College of Medical & Dental Sciences, University of Birmingham, led by Prof Rebecca Drummond. This role is to create and contribute to the creation of knowledge by undertaking a specified range of  activities within an established research programme and/or specific research project.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-22",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10330": {
      "title": "Research Associate - Department of Immunology and Immunotherapy - 108300 - Grade 6",
      "description": "The candidate will provide technical expertise and research support to the Fungal Infection Lab at the University of Birmingham, within the Institute of Immunology & Immunotherapy. The post will be supervised by Professor Rebecca Drummond. The candidate will use animal models of invasive fungal infections and in vitro cultures of immune cells to understand which immune cells and pathways are required for protection against invasive fungal infections.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-15",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10305": {
      "title": "Catalan and Spanish Assistant Language Tutor - Modern Languages - 30901 - Grade 6",
      "description": "The University of Birmingham (UoB), in partnership with the Institut Ramon Lull (IRL), is looking to appoint an 8-month fixed term teaching post in Catalan and Spanish in the Department of Modern Languages. You will contribute to elements of teaching undergraduate and postgraduate students within Catalan and Spanish studies in the Department of Modern Languages. Teaching will be across both the BA in Modern Languages programme and our Institution-wide Languages for All provision.\n\nRole Summary\n\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-19",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10306": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Quantitative Researcher) - School of Social Policy and Society - 108269 - Grade 7",
      "description": "We are seeking to appoint a Quantitative Research Fellow to join the Women, Crime and Justice Research Group. The Group are committed to delivering high-quality research to improve outcomes for women involved in the criminal justice system and to build the evidence base on what works best for them.\nAs part of the Effective Women’s Centre (Phase III) project (JABBS Foundation), the role holder will work across multiple workstreams to turn research questions into analysis plans, carry out the analyses, and write up methods and results for reports and academic papers. In addition, the role holder will also be expected to develop their own lines of research enquiry within the group’s programme, with support.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-29",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10308": {
      "title": "Research Associate - Applied Health Sciences - 108270 - Grade 6",
      "description": "We are looking for a reliable, detail-oriented Student Research Assistant to support Dr Laura Kudrna on an NIHR-funded Programme Grant on Work and Health in Local Government. This is a six-month, part-time hybrid role starting in December. As Student Research Assistant, you’ll support Dr Laura Kudrna on an NIHR-funded Programme Grant on Work and Health in Local Government, alongside other project work as needed. The role will run for six months from December and is hybrid, with one day (7.5 hours) of work per week that can be worked flexibly.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-26",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10309": {
      "title": "Research Associate - Department of Cancer and Genomic Sciences - 108286 - Grade 6",
      "description": "This 1-year position is available to carry out research within a Wellcome Trust-funded research programme, which aims to understand how transcription regulation of genes drives mRNA diversification and diverse mRNA fates. The post holder will carry out independent research in cancer genetics and aim to understand how transcription regulation control mRNA fates upon metabolic stress and metabolic regulation. They will use organoids models to characterise transcriptome profiles of colorectal cancer organoids exposed to various metabolic stresses (hypoxia, mTOR inhibition, nutrient deprivation) and develop novel biomarkers that stratify colorectal cancer organoids responsiveness to mTOR inhibition.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-12",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10319": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Cancer and Genomic Sciences - 108295 - Grade 7",
      "description": "We are seeking an enthusiastic and innovative Research Fellow to join the Centre for Environmental Research and Justice (CERJ) and the Centre for Health Data Science at the Medical School University of Birmingham. You will be working in a vibrant, interdisciplinary research ecosystem, driving cutting-edge research at the intersection of human health and health data Science. This exciting role offers the opportunity to contribute to major EU-funded research programmes, including PARC (Partnership for the Assessment of Risks from Chemicals).\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-12",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10290": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - School of Social Policy and Society - 106899 - Grade 7",
      "description": "We are seeking to immediately recruit a full or part-time research fellow to work until 16th May 2027, remote or hybrid. The post holder will be among the primary researchers on one of the research groups of the Centre for Care: Care Data Infrastructure. They will undertake research under the supervision and guidance of the research group lead, Professor Matt Bennett. The post holder will work closely with colleagues across the consortium, particularly those located at the lead institution (University of Sheffield).\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-18",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10291": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - School of Social Policy and Society - 108260 - Grade 7",
      "description": "The University of Birmingham and the Centre for Care - in partnership with the University of Sheffield - have launched a major new pilot, the Survey of Carers, across selected areas of England. The purpose is to capture data from unpaid carers including those not known to local councils or arranging care privately, to help shape national and local social care policy. \n\nThe project, which started in February 2026, was commissioned by the Department of Health and Social Care (DHSC) and the National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR) and is being led by Professor Matt Bennett at the University of Birmingham and Professor Kate Hamblin at the University of Sheffield. \nThe post holder will be working on the final part of this pilot, evaluating and analysing survey data and producing final reports.\n\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-18",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10302": {
      "title": "Teaching Fellow in Creative Industries - School of English, Drama and Creative Studies - 10302 - Grade 7",
      "description": "The postholder will also undertake personal tutoring and supervise undergraduate and postgraduate taught dissertations. The post will include organisation, management and leadership duties. The successful candidate will have considerable relevant teaching, assessment and professional experience in, for example, creative practice, leadership and project management to contribute to our modules in storytelling and project development. As a full-time Teaching Fellow in Digital Media and Creative Industries, the postholder will be expected to undertake up to 12 hours of timetabled teaching per week at undergraduate and postgraduate level.  \n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-15",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10247": {
      "title": "Research Fellow:  Language Machines Project – English, Drama and Creative Studies- 108223-Grade 7",
      "description": "Join one of three posts on the three-year AHRC-funded project “Language Machines: the Arts & Humanities contributions to Artificial Intelligence Innovation”, led by Dr Rebecca Roach with University of Birmingham co-leads. You’ll map historical networks linking language, meaning, reading and machines around the advent of digital computing, and run experiments exploring generative AI’s impact on reading. Working across disciplines, you’ll develop methods and document findings to inform AI innovation, design, deployment, use and regulation. We welcome humanistic inquiry and interdisciplinary training; expertise in twentieth-century British literature and culture, book history, archival research, quantitative methods, database development or digital history is an advantage.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-22",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10249": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Evaluation of Head Start into Higher Education Programme) - Department of Education and Social Justice - 108232 - Grade 8",
      "description": "To create and disseminate knowledge through initiating and conducting original research and through publication, as appropriate to the evaluation of the Head Start into Higher Education programme which focuses on educational support for care experienced young people. This role will involve supporting an existing evaluation through development and delivery of a participant survey, documentary analysis and case study, as well as supporting writing up of results.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-09",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10282": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Department of Immunology and Immunotherapy - 108258 - Grade 7",
      "description": "To create and contribute to the creation of knowledge by undertaking a specified range of  activities within an established research programme and/or specific research project. This post will be based in the laboratory of Professor Sarah Dimeloe. The research f this group focuses on how the metabolism of immune cells relates to their activity in health and disease.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-23",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10312": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - School of Psychology - 108264 - Grade 7",
      "description": "Applications are invited for a full-time Postdoctoral Research Fellow to join the research programme of Professor Ron Mangun in the Centre for Human Brain Health at the University of Birmingham. The Centre provides a multidisciplinary environment for human cognitive neuroscience research and access to advanced neuroimaging, electrophysiological and brain stimulation methods. The post-holder will contribute to ongoing and planned research investigating visual processing and attention, reading and language processing, and/or predictive coding mechanisms. The successful candidate will have a strong record of high-quality research outputs appropriate to career stage and experience in cognitive neuroscience research. The position is research dedicated, and the successful candidate will be involved in all stages of developing and conducting experiments, analysing data, preparing results, and presenting findings.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-08",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10266": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Department of Cancer and Genomic Sciences - 108203 - Grade 7",
      "description": "We are seeking a Postdoctoral Research Associate to join the group of Dr. Tianyi Zhang based in the Department of Cancer and Genomic Sciences, to investigate how hematopoietic transcription factors and epigenetic regulators control B cell function and how their dysregulation contribute to blood cancers.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-12-06",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10315": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - School of Engineering - 108276 - Grade 7",
      "description": "To create and contribute to the creation of knowledge by undertaking a specified range of activities within an established research programme and/or specific research project.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-17",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10318": {
      "title": "Applied Memory Lab Research Associate - School of Psychology - 108292 - Grade 6",
      "description": "A Research Associate (RA) is a junior/entry-level research-focused role with a global remit. Your main responsibility is to support other members of the Applied Memory lab on project work for a diverse range of studies and impact activities. You may also be tasked with liaising with study participants directly and working with other senior team members to ensure the efficient and effective coordination of project work.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-17",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10246": {
      "title": "Research Fellow in Theoretical Physics - College of Engineering and Physical Sciences - 105029 - Grade 7",
      "description": "Applications are invited for a postdoctoral research position in the Theoretical Physics group at the University of Birmingham, working in the research team of Prof. Hannah Price as part of the EPSRC Programme Grant “Quantum Advantage In Quantitative Quantum Simulation (QQQS)”. This full-time position is for 24 months, with the possibility of extension. The ideal start-date is 1st May 2027. We seek a highly-motivated individual with a theoretical background primarily in one or more of: ultracold atoms, condensed matter physics or quantum information. The successful candidate will develop theoretical approaches and perform computational calculations for quantum many-body physics. This project involves a high degree of teamwork and interdisciplinary research, including collaborations with other members of Prof. Price’s research group as well as with other UK theoretical and experimental groups as part of the QQQS programme grant. \n\nPosting closes: 2026-12-02",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10313": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - School of Psychology - 108265 - Grade 7",
      "description": "The post-holder will contribute to ongoing and planned research investigating visual processing and attention, reading and language processing, and/or predictive coding mechanisms. The successful candidate will have a strong record of high-quality research outputs appropriate to career stage and experience in cognitive neuroscience research. The position is research dedicated, and the successful candidate will be involved in all stages of developing and conducting experiments, analysing data, preparing results, and presenting findings. Applications are invited for a full-time Postdoctoral Research Fellow to join the research programme of Professor Ron Mangun in the Centre for Human Brain Health at the University of Birmingham. \n\nPosting closes: 2026-12-02",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10339": {
      "title": "Anatomy Demonstrator - School of Biomedical Sciences - 98169 - Grade 6",
      "description": "The University of Birmingham is offering the role of Anatomy Demonstrator(s) to suitably qualified individuals wishing to develop their skills in teaching anatomy as a basis for further career development. Their main responsibility will be to teach anatomy by means of small group teaching sessions and demonstration of prosected cadaveric material. Anatomy demonstrators are part of the anatomy teaching delivery team for undergraduate and postgraduate Medical, Dental, Pharmacy, Nursing, Physiotherapy, Physician Associate and Biomedical Sciences students in modularised programmes of the College of Medicine and Health.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-12-02",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10342": {
      "title": "Research Fellow in Cosmology with Transients - School of Physics and Astronomy - 108253 - Grade 7",
      "description": "The position is open to work with the group of  Dr. Suhail Dhawan on the UKRI/ERC project NGCOSMO. \nThe projects can include (but not limited to): \n•\tInference of H0 with strong gravitationally lensed supernovae\n•\tThe local distance ladder measurement of H0\n•\tDark energy inference with Supernovae\n•\tSynergies between LSST and Euclid surveys \n\nWe are members of LSST and Euclid and the applicant will also have access to independent programs with SOAR, Liverpool telescope, GTC, VLT and 4MOST as well as JWST/HST programs as part of large and diverse international collaborations. There are ample supercomputing resources from both local and international collaborative facilities. The position comes with a generous allowance to cover travels to conferences and research   visits,  and   guaranteed   access   to   the   university’s   \nhigh-performance supercomputer BlueBEAR. Additionally, the successful candidate will have the opportunity to supervise students, acquire teaching experience,\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-25",
      "department": null
    },
    "https://edzz.fa.em3.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_6001/job/10344": {
      "title": "Research Fellow (Postdoctoral) - School of Social Policy and Society - 108219 - Grade 7",
      "description": "To create and contribute to the creation of knowledge by undertaking research on suicide and homicide risk among young carers.\n\nPosting closes: 2026-11-25",
      "department": null
    }
  },
